00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:33.960
of all the lessons we've done.  Alright, here it is...

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:38.040
Mr. Sejii's first photo.

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:43.400
This image should remind you

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:48.880
that we are in the midst of a practice

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:51.800
for people of moderate capacity

00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:53.920
and what they are trying to achieve is nirvana.

00:01:54.040 --> 00:02:00.200
They try to get out of the wheel of life, from all the suffering for themselves personally.  This is

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:04.040
where the Buddha taught three trainings

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:08.520
that will help you achieve your personal nirvana.  The

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:13.880
third practice is understanding emptiness, understanding the pen.  The

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:17.240
second training is meditation.

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:22.600
On a deep level, both of these can only be done in a quiet place,

00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:28.240
at a specific time of day, when you are completely focused on the meditation cushion.

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:33.080
At a deeper level, both should be done

00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:36.200
at specific periods of the day.

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:41.040
But the first, the basis of the second is to be kind to others.

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:42.720
You could call it morality.

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:45.200
You can call it an ethical way of life,

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:50.120
but ultimately it is about doing good to others.

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:52.200
That is the foundation,

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:55.160
which is always available to us throughout the day.

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:59.240
This is one of the three great trainings of Buddhism,

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:02.160
aimed at helping us attain nirvana.

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:05.440
And it is available to us all day long.

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:06.800
So in this picture,

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:11.800
you can see Seiji helping Geshe Michael use his computer.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:16.160
Which is one of the best things a young person can do for an old person.

