00:21:30.520 --> 00:21:32.800
and we have peaches now.

00:21:35.080 --> 00:21:40.160
What that means is, keep your basic practices.

00:21:40.160 --> 00:21:44.560
Take care of the roots, and plants of good karma

00:21:45.200 --> 00:21:47.920
by keeping your vows, by being kind to others.

00:21:47.920 --> 00:21:49.960
Then it will grow into a tree.

00:21:50.440 --> 00:21:52.440
And the peach tree we planted

00:21:53.200 --> 00:21:55.080
five months ago or something,

00:21:55.080 --> 00:21:58.040
is already bearing a lot of fruit.

00:21:58.600 --> 00:22:05.040
If you don't take care of it when it's small, you'll have nothing.

00:22:05.040 --> 00:22:08.200
If you take care of your basic Buddhist practice,

00:22:08.800 --> 00:22:10.800
which is being kind to others,

00:22:11.400 --> 00:22:14.120
then the fruits will be thousands and thousands and thousands.

00:22:14.200 --> 00:22:16.160
It will come, it will grow

00:22:16.160 --> 00:22:18.160
big... it will grow into a tree

00:22:18.600 --> 00:22:23.480
that will give peaches every year and for many years you will have peaches.

00:22:24.160 --> 00:22:25.560
Take care...protect....

00:22:25.760 --> 00:22:29.560
This child protects the bud carefully.

00:22:29.960 --> 00:22:31.960
Protect your morality.

00:22:32.520 --> 00:22:34.520
Next image.

00:22:36.240 --> 00:22:41.320
If I remember correctly, there are four conditions

00:22:42.240 --> 00:22:45.080
that can cause you to break your commitment.

00:22:45.080 --> 00:22:47.080
If you take the bodhisattva commitment

00:22:47.840 --> 00:22:50.440
or you take the vinaya pratimoksha commitment,

00:22:51.000 --> 00:22:53.840
or even if you take the diamond path tantric commitment.

00:22:54.800 --> 00:23:00.200
I think there are four.  Pabongka Rinpoche reviewed... maybe more than that....

00:23:01.000 --> 00:23:02.920
basically, there are certain conditions

00:23:03.000 --> 00:23:05.080
that will help you break your vows.

00:23:05.160 --> 00:23:09.240
If you want to break your vow, there are some specific ways to do it.

00:23:09.240 --> 00:23:10.320
The first;

00:23:11.080 --> 00:23:16.440
that is, if you don't know what your vows are,

00:23:17.120 --> 00:23:21.000
that's a great way to break them.  If you want to break them,

00:23:21.000 --> 00:23:22.720
then don't study them and,

00:23:23.160 --> 00:23:27.080
one of the annoying things, I have a lot of annoying things about the dharma,

00:23:28.160 --> 00:23:33.800
is teachers who give big initiations,

00:23:33.800 --> 00:23:38.600
and they don't explain to the people who are taking the initiation

00:23:39.080 --> 00:23:41.520
that they have just taken vows.

00:23:41.560 --> 00:23:44.840
There are hundreds of vows you take when you get initiated,

00:23:45.760 --> 00:23:48.320
and you will break them if you don't know them.

00:23:48.320 --> 00:23:51.120
It is the teacher's responsibility

00:23:52.120 --> 00:23:55.400
to train you in your vows before you receive the initiation ceremony.

00:23:56.320 --> 00:24:01.080
If they don't offer to train you, I wouldn't take initiation from them.  The

00:24:02.120 --> 00:24:07.080
best way to break your vows, the first way, is to not know them.

00:24:07.560 --> 00:24:09.400
Read the recipe before you start cooking.

00:24:10.240 --> 00:24:12.720
That's what Veronica says every time I cook.

00:24:14.160 --> 00:24:16.160
Next image.

00:24:17.000 --> 00:24:23.360
It was a woman who said, 'Yeah, it's no big deal'.

00:24:23.560 --> 00:24:33.600
A vow not to cut greenery without a prayer,

00:24:34.320 --> 00:24:40.400
come on, that's a bit extreme.  That's a bit too much, not so important.

00:24:40.400 --> 00:24:43.000
Only a few insects

00:24:43.000 --> 00:24:47.560
may use the leaves occasionally as a roof.

00:24:47.560 --> 00:24:50.040
It's not a big deal.  The

00:24:50.480 --> 00:24:53.800
second best way to break your vow

00:24:54.040 --> 00:24:55.400
is to have this attitude;

00:24:55.400 --> 00:24:59.200
'Oh that one isn't that important, I'm looking after the big one.'

00:25:00.200 --> 00:25:02.120
Next.

00:25:06.240 --> 00:25:12.400
If we get klesha, meaning if we have some negativity

00:25:12.800 --> 00:25:16.920
in our mind, it is a great way to break your vows.

00:25:17.080 --> 00:25:20.600
Feeling annoyed with other people or

00:25:21.080 --> 00:25:26.280
obsessed with getting something or money or

00:25:26.600 --> 00:25:29.480
addicted to Netflix at night.

00:25:30.040 --> 00:25:36.000
.... by the way, it's not wrong to watch Netflix, but I'm talking about

00:25:38.960 --> 00:25:43.200
hurting other people because you want to go home and watch Netflix.  That's a problem.

00:25:44.800 --> 00:25:46.920
This is called a gang fight.

00:25:46.920 --> 00:25:48.320
What's the story?

00:25:52.120 --> 00:25:56.040
Attacking the biggest person on the other side.

00:25:57.000 --> 00:25:59.000
Find out who the leader of the other side is,

00:25:59.560 --> 00:26:04.080
and don't talk, don't negotiate, don't shout at each other,

00:26:04.080 --> 00:26:07.000
walk up to him and hit him on the head.

00:26:07.480 --> 00:26:10.800
And then the whole other side will collapse.

00:26:11.080 --> 00:26:15.080
Identify your worst habits,

00:26:15.080 --> 00:26:19.000
and attack them first.  It's a way to keep your vows.

00:26:19.760 --> 00:26:21.760
Next.

00:26:25.240 --> 00:26:30.640
.... by the way at my age,

00:26:30.640 --> 00:26:33.760
I'm not saying how old I am,

00:26:33.760 --> 00:26:37.080
but all this young love is

00:26:37.080 --> 00:26:40.160
so ridiculous from my age perspective.

00:26:42.320 --> 00:26:44.800
I can say that with experience because I have it.

00:26:46.320 --> 00:26:48.240
But this thing about,

00:26:48.240 --> 00:26:50.800
oh, she's the most beautiful woman in the world.

00:26:51.400 --> 00:26:53.400
He is the most handsome man in the world.

00:26:54.440 --> 00:26:59.560
First of all, my oldest brother,

00:26:59.560 --> 00:27:02.920
he said the funniest thing.  He said, do you like that girl?  I said, yes.

00:27:03.480 --> 00:27:05.480
He said, you want to spend your life with him?  I said, yes.

00:27:06.160 --> 00:27:08.160
He said, check on his mother first.

00:27:09.000 --> 00:27:16.120
See what her mother looks like?  I said, Mom looks terrible.  He was overweight, he looked tired and he looked terrible.

00:27:16.920 --> 00:27:21.800
And he said, well, what do you think he used to look like,

00:27:22.040 --> 00:27:24.240
So think about this?

00:27:25.480 --> 00:27:29.560
If you are attached to someone's appearance,

00:27:30.240 --> 00:27:35.280
or something physical, or something less important about someone.

00:27:35.480 --> 00:27:41.120
It will change and you will see them get sick,

00:27:41.120 --> 00:27:44.000
you will see them get old.  You will see them having diarrhea and vomiting.

00:27:44.240 --> 00:27:48.040
If you are unlucky you will see them inside and in operation sometime.

00:27:49.080 --> 00:27:52.120
Don't fool yourself

00:27:53.080 --> 00:27:55.080
that it's worth hurting others

00:27:55.760 --> 00:28:00.680
to get the most beautiful woman or man.  This is not worth it.

00:28:01.960 --> 00:28:08.600
This won't last long.  It's nice to have a relationship but have it for the right reasons.

00:28:09.200 --> 00:28:11.200
Next.

00:28:13.000 --> 00:28:15.080
If you have problems with anger

00:28:16.160 --> 00:28:18.160
or you get angry easily.

00:28:18.320 --> 00:28:21.080
Try fantasizing about giving this person

00:28:21.760 --> 00:28:25.480
something they would love to have.  This is called maitri,

00:28:26.120 --> 00:28:27.480
jampa,

00:28:27.480 --> 00:28:28.120
love.

00:28:28.120 --> 00:28:33.400
Fantasizing, trying to remember how good it would be to give someone...

00:28:34.040 --> 00:28:36.160
something they love, something they want.

00:28:36.200 --> 00:28:38.240
Try to have this attitude.

00:28:38.720 --> 00:28:42.040
If you don't feel friendly towards others

00:28:43.000 --> 00:28:45.880
then do some fantasy, which means meditating

00:28:47.000 --> 00:28:50.440
on giving them something they would really like.

00:28:51.000 --> 00:28:53.000
Next.

00:28:54.040 --> 00:29:00.040
I'll give you some time on this one.  I bet you don't remember what this one is?

00:29:01.480 --> 00:29:03.400
The team cheated by looking ahead.

00:29:08.040 --> 00:29:10.040
What is this one?

00:29:11.080 --> 00:29:13.960
This is about pride.

00:29:14.720 --> 00:29:17.840
Pride will also be an obstacle to keeping your vows.

00:29:18.720 --> 00:29:22.120
And... one of the most common types of pride

00:29:23.000 --> 00:29:28.040
in the monastic context, where this book is commonly taught;

00:29:30.320 --> 00:29:35.280
is how much you know about ancient scriptures, how many facts you have collected

00:29:36.040 --> 00:29:37.120
in life.

00:29:37.400 --> 00:29:41.280
This is something I really enjoy, about the understanding of dharma

00:29:41.280 --> 00:29:43.080
and the more you collect

00:29:43.480 --> 00:29:47.080
the more special you feel.

00:29:48.040 --> 00:29:52.960
Pabongka Rinpoche said, 'All the dharma you've ever studied in your life, all the things you've memorized,

00:29:52.960 --> 00:29:54.720
all the things you've debated,

00:29:54.720 --> 00:29:56.800
all the geshe titles you've ever had,

00:29:58.480 --> 00:30:04.160
compared to what's left to know, you know nothing.

00:30:04.480 --> 00:30:07.560
You are like a worm at the bottom of the sea,

00:30:08.240 --> 00:30:10.120
and sometimes you come out and look at the stars.

00:30:13.000 --> 00:30:15.680
Many stars have planets around them.

00:30:16.520 --> 00:30:20.440
There are people on those planets.  There are things to know about those people.

00:30:21.400 --> 00:30:24.480
There are things we know,

00:30:24.720 --> 00:30:26.720
that we are so proud of,

00:30:27.680 --> 00:30:33.880
that are a small fraction of what you can know.

00:30:35.160 --> 00:30:37.200
So don't be arrogant.

00:30:37.200 --> 00:30:39.200
Next.

00:30:43.000 --> 00:30:47.240
One of the big motivations for breaking your vows

00:30:47.680 --> 00:30:54.240
or your commitments is morality, which will stop you from attaining nirvana, which will stop you from attaining both

00:30:55.080 --> 00:30:57.680
levels of the lamrim - personal nirvana;

00:30:58.720 --> 00:31:03.000
is to understand emptiness, to study emptiness.

00:31:04.320 --> 00:31:06.320
If you realize, that the evil things

00:31:06.920 --> 00:31:08.920
that other people do to you,

00:31:09.480 --> 00:31:13.240
come directly from what you did last week.

00:31:13.960 --> 00:31:18.240
Then you won't make a big mistake.  The more you can learn about emptiness,

00:31:19.000 --> 00:31:22.440
the more you can learn about cause and effect, the initial dependence

00:31:23.000 --> 00:31:25.280
that means this person comes from my seed,

00:31:26.360 --> 00:31:33.760
then it will be easier to keep your vows.  It's getting easier to maintain.  So study, study, study.

00:31:35.560 --> 00:31:41.320
I had a teacher, an old Mongolian teacher, who was very old with tuberculosis and

00:31:46.800 --> 00:31:48.720
he used to say,

00:31:48.720 --> 00:31:56.240
'He is very good.  You're so proud, you have a huge amount of pride from Princeton and

00:31:57.080 --> 00:31:58.720
then the geshe,

00:31:58.720 --> 00:32:00.800
it really, really helps...

00:32:00.880 --> 00:32:03.960
You'll push yourself harder

00:32:04.440 --> 00:32:06.440
just to look smart.

00:32:06.520 --> 00:32:11.600
That's lucky, but later try to give up.

00:32:11.960 --> 00:32:15.080
Just learn to be a good person.  This is so funny

00:32:16.080 --> 00:32:19.000
He gave me Adam's text on his deathbed.

00:32:19.760 --> 00:32:21.760
I remember this.

00:32:24.040 --> 00:32:25.960
Next.

00:32:25.960 --> 00:32:30.320
This is technically the fourth cause.  No.

00:32:30.440 --> 00:32:35.480
One of the reasons for breaking your vows or losing your commitment.  It is

00:32:37.560 --> 00:32:39.680
very difficult in the modern world

00:32:40.120 --> 00:32:45.960
to keep your mind on the promise when you are very busy.  When things move very fast.

00:32:46.520 --> 00:32:48.920
There are a thousand things to see on the internet,

00:32:49.680 --> 00:32:53.000
and life moves so fast.  It

00:32:53.440 --> 00:32:58.640
's hard to maintain self-awareness;

00:32:58.640 --> 00:33:03.080
did I break an oath, did I do something to hurt someone?

00:33:03.840 --> 00:33:08.680
You have to slow down, go back to your vows

00:33:09.080 --> 00:33:14.720
and have some kind of sensitive awareness

00:33:15.000 --> 00:33:19.880
of the fact that you have a commitment not to hurt others.

00:33:20.080 --> 00:33:24.160
The busier you are, the more careful you have to be.

00:33:25.680 --> 00:33:31.000
It's easy to get annoyed with your colleagues when you're busy.

00:33:31.000 --> 00:33:33.200
They're trying to tell you something and

00:33:33.960 --> 00:33:36.320
you've got 10 things going on at work and you're...

00:33:37.840 --> 00:33:42.120
'I don't have time to listen right now.

00:33:42.800 --> 00:33:45.960
My boss gave me 10 things to do.'

00:33:46.440 --> 00:33:48.440
That's when you have to slow down

00:33:49.200 --> 00:33:51.200
and go back to your vows.

00:33:51.280 --> 00:33:55.000
Don't forget your commitment to be kind to others even when you are

00:33:55.680 --> 00:33:57.680
very stressed, very busy.  It is

00:33:59.960 --> 00:34:04.440
better to break some business commitments than to be

00:34:05.760 --> 00:34:10.040
nervous and stressed and unkind to people,

00:34:11.200 --> 00:34:14.040
it is better not to pay a bill or miss a business meeting or

00:34:15.000 --> 00:34:17.560
not do as well as you can at work,

00:34:18.720 --> 00:34:21.960
if it means keeping your mind clear.

00:34:25.080 --> 00:34:27.080
Next image.

00:34:27.480 --> 00:34:30.840
This is a woman who buys useless things in a shop.

00:34:33.200 --> 00:34:35.200
See if you remember this story.

00:34:36.800 --> 00:34:42.160
He said, 'Oh this box is so beautiful.  He went to the mall.  He bought this .....

00:34:42.600 --> 00:34:44.600
.... what is a home improvement store,

00:34:45.080 --> 00:34:48.480
where you buy things?  Crate and Barrel.

00:34:49.000 --> 00:34:54.040
He went to Crate and Barrel in America.  She said, 'Oh my husband will love this box.'

00:34:54.520 --> 00:34:57.480
He didn't know what he would use it for

00:34:58.040 --> 00:35:00.040
but he would take it home.

00:35:04.320 --> 00:35:09.400
Then when she came home, her husband would say, 'You're crazy, this is a worthless little box.

00:35:09.400 --> 00:35:15.480
We have a lot of trash at home.  Return.  Get your money back.

00:35:16.920 --> 00:35:20.720
Should he go to the gas station and try to return it?

00:35:24.120 --> 00:35:29.760
No, that's not where he bought the box.  This is a bit obvious but we have to say it.

00:35:31.480 --> 00:35:33.480
If you buy a stupid box,

00:35:34.040 --> 00:35:37.080
because you like it and you think your husband will like it, which turns out he doesn't...

00:35:39.000 --> 00:35:41.080
And he asks you to return the box.

00:35:42.040 --> 00:35:46.160
Don't take it back to a different place.  Take it back to where you bought it.

00:35:46.720 --> 00:35:48.720
What does it mean?

00:35:55.480 --> 00:35:58.080
You have to pay me.

00:35:59.680 --> 00:36:01.680
When you are in confession,

00:36:01.680 --> 00:36:03.480
if you break a vow,

00:36:03.480 --> 00:36:06.120
try to go back to the person who gave you the vow.

00:36:07.080 --> 00:36:12.120
Try to confess in front of the person who gave you the oath.

00:36:12.200 --> 00:36:15.960
Can you confess in your own home?

00:36:17.680 --> 00:36:21.960
Not for the oaths you take from others, in general.

00:36:24.040 --> 00:36:26.040
If you don't take vows

00:36:26.040 --> 00:36:28.600
from others, then it might be okay at home

00:36:29.280 --> 00:36:34.080
to confess in front of a Buddha statue or something like that, in extreme cases it's okay.

00:36:34.440 --> 00:36:36.120
But in general,

00:36:36.520 --> 00:36:39.080
if you can go back to the person who gave you your vows,

00:36:40.160 --> 00:36:45.200
confess your sins to them openly - don't be shy.  We are not shy all day long.

00:36:45.840 --> 00:36:49.080
Therefore, do not be shy about your oath, and say 'why is that'

00:36:49.960 --> 00:36:52.720
go directly to your teacher and say I broke this stupid oath.

00:36:53.200 --> 00:36:56.720
And your teacher is 'wow, you're such a bad person.'  You're like, yeah, yeah.

00:36:57.400 --> 00:37:02.040
Get over it, then you feel clean, you feel good.

00:37:03.520 --> 00:37:07.320
You can be shy about many things in life, but don't be shy about your vows.

00:37:07.320 --> 00:37:11.000
If you break an oath, go tell someone

00:37:11.000 --> 00:37:14.240
and that's how you get rid of it.  You get rid of the problem.

00:37:14.520 --> 00:37:20.000
If you hold onto it and hide it, and if you spend more time hiding it than admitting it

00:37:20.040 --> 00:37:23.200
or keeping it, then that's stupid

00:37:23.480 --> 00:37:26.600
and you won't feel good.  You won't feel clean.

00:37:27.480 --> 00:37:31.760
Be open with your teacher.  I have this problem.  I have a bad habit.

00:37:33.560 --> 00:37:37.720
Karma will be destroyed, seeds will be destroyed.

00:37:38.320 --> 00:37:44.920
Your teacher will say, "I heard that before, you told me."  But you have to be persistent and keep telling them.  The

00:37:48.320 --> 00:37:50.320
next picture

00:37:51.840 --> 00:37:54.320
is about .....wait, do you remember?

00:38:01.160 --> 00:38:04.200
Again, it's about respecting the

00:38:04.800 --> 00:38:07.480
small details of the vows.

00:38:08.400 --> 00:38:13.680
This is actually a vow for monks, they have to brush their teeth,

00:38:13.680 --> 00:38:16.320
with a stick called so shing (SO SHING)

00:38:16.320 --> 00:38:18.440
it is a stick that you are supposed to use to clean your teeth,

00:38:18.600 --> 00:38:21.280
you just cut it from a tree and use it.

00:38:22.160 --> 00:38:24.160
This is a toothbrush.

00:38:24.320 --> 00:38:29.360
He said, monks should have toothbrushes and you should brush your teeth.

00:38:31.840 --> 00:38:34.040
This may seem like a small thing;

00:38:34.920 --> 00:38:38.920
"Wait, I'm trying to keep my tantric vow to go to Amitabha's heaven"

00:38:39.560 --> 00:38:43.080
and protect all sentient beings and Buddha said, 'Yes, but in the meantime,

00:38:43.080 --> 00:38:46.240
could you brush your teeth every day.

00:38:46.240 --> 00:38:49.560
You think, but that's not really a big vow.

00:38:50.040 --> 00:38:53.800
But it's the little things that make a buddhist paradise.

00:38:53.800 --> 00:38:57.680
These are the little things that Bodhisattvas do,

00:38:58.040 --> 00:39:00.120
which is being kind to others.

00:39:01.000 --> 00:39:03.840
Of course, everyone in the world would...

00:39:05.080 --> 00:39:09.000
...stop a nuclear war or something if they could.  I mean, that's obvious.

00:39:10.160 --> 00:39:12.120
But are you a good enough person,

00:39:13.200 --> 00:39:15.840
that you don't even want people to smell your breath?

00:39:16.800 --> 00:39:18.360
If it might hurt them?

00:39:18.480 --> 00:39:20.160
If you are very sensitive

00:39:21.080 --> 00:39:23.560
about small things that might hurt others,

00:39:24.920 --> 00:39:27.200
then we can say you are guarding your morals.

00:39:28.160 --> 00:39:33.680
And then it's the little details that put the finishing touches

00:39:34.240 --> 00:39:37.560
on your buddha paradise, which you see in the next picture.

00:39:41.480 --> 00:39:46.160
This guy decorated a Christmas tree...

00:39:47.800 --> 00:39:52.240
If you've ever done a Christmas tree, but those of us who were raised in the Christian tradition,

00:39:53.000 --> 00:39:55.000
our parents made us make a Christmas tree.

00:39:55.840 --> 00:39:58.120
There's something cool about

00:39:58.920 --> 00:40:01.800
putting the last ornament on.

00:40:01.800 --> 00:40:06.920
Everyone looked at the tree and they said, 'Is it finished' and they said, 'Yes, it's finished'.

00:40:07.840 --> 00:40:11.480
He said, 'Wait, there's one more thing we have to put in there'.

00:40:12.040 --> 00:40:14.800
This Christmas tree decoration

00:40:16.040 --> 00:40:22.000
is brushing your teeth.  This is the last little detail

00:40:22.240 --> 00:40:28.720
that means you are putting your Buddhahood.  These are the little things that make a Buddha.

00:40:28.720 --> 00:40:32.160
This is not a big deal.  It's not a big deal.  It is attention

00:40:33.080 --> 00:40:35.000
to the small details of

00:40:35.000 --> 00:40:40.120
making others happy that creates buddhas.

00:40:41.560 --> 00:40:43.560
Next.

00:40:45.560 --> 00:40:49.040
See if you remember this one.  I'll give you a hint - yamantaka, yamantaka.

00:40:57.000 --> 00:40:59.960
This is the famous lamrim story.

00:41:01.960 --> 00:41:06.040
Monks and nuns must attend sojong twice a month and confess their

00:41:06.920 --> 00:41:08.920
wrongdoings to each other

00:41:09.400 --> 00:41:11.400
openly.

00:41:13.080 --> 00:41:15.080
The teacher said,

00:41:15.200 --> 00:41:18.320
...they hit gunty.  They hit a gunty

00:41:19.200 --> 00:41:22.600
which is a special piece of wood, looks like a 2x4

00:41:23.200 --> 00:41:27.600
and you hit it with another stick and it goes thunk, thunk, thunk...

00:41:28.160 --> 00:41:33.400
and it was an old fashioned bell before metal became common.

00:41:33.400 --> 00:41:38.080
They would hit the board, and when you heard it

00:41:38.240 --> 00:41:41.360
you had to go to the sojong.  They still do it.

00:41:41.680 --> 00:41:44.040
I made gunty with my teacher.  He wanted one

00:41:45.200 --> 00:41:47.560
and we made it to the exact dimensions.

00:41:47.960 --> 00:41:49.600
There are all these rules about it.

00:41:49.880 --> 00:41:51.880
When you hear gunty

00:41:52.240 --> 00:41:54.240
you should.... you hold it here..

00:41:54.600 --> 00:41:57.360
you hold the gunty here and you hit it like this.

00:41:58.040 --> 00:42:01.200
Then all the monks and nuns should come to confession.

00:42:02.120 --> 00:42:05.760
This teacher said, 'hey, they hit gunty.  Come on.'

00:42:06.520 --> 00:42:09.200
The students said, 'No, I will not confess today.'

00:42:10.160 --> 00:42:12.160
The teacher said, 'What?'

00:42:12.440 --> 00:42:17.200
It is one of the main commitments of a monk, to go to sojong.

00:42:17.960 --> 00:42:20.600
The teacher said, 'What are you talking about?'  He said, 'I don't need to go today.'

00:42:21.400 --> 00:42:24.080
The teacher said, 'What do you mean you don't have to go today?'

00:42:24.120 --> 00:42:27.920
He said, 'Did you forget, you gave me a yamantaka initiation yesterday?

00:42:28.320 --> 00:42:33.080
I am yamantaka, I am Buddha.  I don't need to go to Sojong anymore.'  The

00:42:33.960 --> 00:42:38.160
teacher pulled his ears, saying, 'What is this, you yamantika?

00:42:38.280 --> 00:42:43.240
Yamantika will go to sojong with me now.'

00:42:44.600 --> 00:42:48.160
What it means is, don't give me the excuse that you are a great tantrika,

00:42:49.080 --> 00:42:51.640
and you are above morality and

00:42:51.640 --> 00:42:54.080
now you have a higher vision -

00:42:54.800 --> 00:42:57.960
that is a completely wrong idea!

00:42:58.920 --> 00:43:02.040
If you have a secret initiation

00:43:02.600 --> 00:43:05.600
then you have to go to sojong every morning or something.

00:43:05.840 --> 00:43:08.400
You have to go further than anyone else.

00:43:08.400 --> 00:43:10.760
Because that's what gives you...

00:43:11.000 --> 00:43:14.920
gives power to your tantra practice.  Treat others well

00:43:14.920 --> 00:43:16.720
and admit when you make a mistake.

00:43:17.480 --> 00:43:19.480
Next.

00:43:22.520 --> 00:43:29.080
This is a sad picture.  We always think of morality as the root

00:43:29.080 --> 00:43:32.120
of our practice, the basis of our practice.

00:43:33.120 --> 00:43:35.960
Pabongka Rinpoche, kind of flipped it around.

00:43:37.000 --> 00:43:38.800
This is a perfect picture.

00:43:38.800 --> 00:43:42.240
He said, imagine an apple tree

00:43:42.440 --> 00:43:46.160
that has been cut in half.  Actually, he used a palm tree.

00:43:47.400 --> 00:43:52.360
Someone sliced ​​and cut the top of the tree.

00:43:52.720 --> 00:43:55.080
So you won't get any leaves, not

00:43:55.360 --> 00:43:58.040
even a single leaf will come out.

00:43:58.320 --> 00:44:00.440
Therefore, you will not earn interest.

00:44:01.480 --> 00:44:05.080
Therefore, you will not get the fruits that always come from the flowers.

00:44:05.840 --> 00:44:07.880
You will get nothing.

00:44:08.160 --> 00:44:13.560
A person who is unkind to others day after day, hour after hour,

00:44:14.800 --> 00:44:18.840
they cut off every opportunity

00:44:20.160 --> 00:44:23.560
to gain the beautiful fruits of practice.

00:44:23.680 --> 00:44:25.200
Next.

00:44:32.160 --> 00:44:34.920
This is an idea from something my teacher asked me...

00:44:36.800 --> 00:44:42.440
Sorry, I asked my teacher and I don't know if you remember but I asked him.

00:44:44.040 --> 00:44:49.200
The first of the five paths, the path of accumulation,

00:44:50.800 --> 00:44:55.440
you attain it when you have personal tragedy,

00:44:55.840 --> 00:44:59.080
but if you are on the bodhisattva path,

00:44:59.400 --> 00:45:01.560
you attain it when you gain bodhichitta.

00:45:01.560 --> 00:45:05.680
I said, I don't understand what's tragic about bodhichitta?

00:45:07.000 --> 00:45:09.000
And he said, 'No, no, no.

00:45:09.280 --> 00:45:12.440
This is still a tragedy theme.

00:45:13.000 --> 00:45:19.200
The tragedy of every living creature, every creature in the entire universe is

00:45:20.120 --> 00:45:22.120
experiencing the same tragedy.'

00:45:23.440 --> 00:45:30.000
Communal tragedy is the beginning of five paths.

00:45:30.160 --> 00:45:32.200
Thinking about the tragedy

00:45:32.520 --> 00:45:35.600
is the beginning of the five paths for a bodhisattva.

00:45:35.600 --> 00:45:37.120
So yes, it is the same.  The

00:45:37.560 --> 00:45:41.760
puppy was having a hard time, but now all the puppies in the basket were having a hard time.

00:45:44.040 --> 00:45:46.040
We are all in this together.

00:45:46.040 --> 00:45:48.800
And that is the beginning of bodhichitta.

00:45:50.160 --> 00:45:53.560
Next image.

00:45:53.560 --> 00:45:58.200
This is a man shaking hands with someone in their office.

00:45:58.920 --> 00:46:05.200
I imagined the woman introducing them.  This is Joe, he works in the advertising department.

00:46:05.200 --> 00:46:08.800
and this is Sam, he works in the computer department.

00:46:09.400 --> 00:46:11.400
They shook hands.  Do

00:46:12.040 --> 00:46:14.040
you remember what this is?

00:46:19.000 --> 00:46:24.520
It was a very, very funny exercise where we were supposed to close our eyes

00:46:25.280 --> 00:46:28.160
and think of the person who annoys us the most.

00:46:28.920 --> 00:46:33.120
And see if we can feel the anger.  The problem with exercises like this

00:46:33.760 --> 00:46:36.240
is that after about 10 minutes you forget it's an exercise.

00:46:37.080 --> 00:46:39.080
You're really getting angry!

00:46:40.160 --> 00:46:42.160
Let me see if I can make myself angry.

00:46:42.600 --> 00:46:44.160
How would you do it?

00:46:44.160 --> 00:46:46.920
I'm going to think about this person who gave me a hard time this week.  'Okay, go ahead'.

00:46:48.440 --> 00:46:52.320
Then slowly the person started to tremble.  You ask, 'What happened?'

00:46:52.480 --> 00:46:56.040
I'm angry. The experiment worked.

00:46:56.800 --> 00:47:00.400
If it were your 'old', they would say,

00:47:01.080 --> 00:47:05.000
'check what it felt like the first time you thought about this person.'

00:47:06.040 --> 00:47:08.600
How does it feel? What arises in your heart?

00:47:09.480 --> 00:47:13.040
I don't know about you, but I experience a little bit of irritation in my heart.

00:47:13.080 --> 00:47:17.960
I start to feel a kind of discomfort here or there.

00:47:18.600 --> 00:47:23.080
When I think about someone who has bothered me or a problem that has bothered me,

00:47:23.680 --> 00:47:27.480
I can intentionally generate tension

00:47:27.760 --> 00:47:29.760
within myself.

00:47:30.120 --> 00:47:36.920
He said, 'Let's practice—try to trigger some tension in your heart,

00:47:37.280 --> 00:47:42.040
then notice that tension and recognize it, as if you were shaking hands with someone.

00:47:43.000 --> 00:47:46.600
Recognize what it feels like

00:47:47.000 --> 00:47:50.040
when mental suffering, negative emotions

00:47:51.000 --> 00:47:54.240
first arise in your heart and keep practicing.

00:47:55.200 --> 00:47:58.040
As soon as you feel better, and you forget about this person,

00:47:58.040 --> 00:47:59.200
then think about them again.

00:48:00.200 --> 00:48:01.520
See if you can get angry again.

00:48:01.520 --> 00:48:03.360
See if you can start getting angry again.

00:48:04.040 --> 00:48:08.840
Try to become familiar with what it feels like, shaking hands. 'Hi. This is Geshe Michael.

00:48:08.840 --> 00:48:10.320
Hi. What's your name?

00:48:11.080 --> 00:48:14.080
I'm starting to get upset with this person.

00:48:14.080 --> 00:48:17.000
Nice to meet you. Now I know what you look like.

00:48:17.680 --> 00:48:21.200
Now I can be careful. I can avoid you in the future.'

00:48:21.840 --> 00:48:23.840
Next.

00:48:28.240 --> 00:48:30.920
This is called visiting the middle of the sun.

00:48:33.000 --> 00:48:37.960
This lamrim theme, which is Love in the Time of Viruses.

00:48:41.080 --> 00:48:44.320
Viruses are a big thing,  and it's spreading all over the world.

00:48:45.000 --> 00:48:48.320
I've lived a long time and I thought I'd seen it all.

00:48:49.080 --> 00:48:54.960
I was entering my 60s and thought by now nothing new was going to happen.

00:48:55.120 --> 00:48:57.400
I was pretty much prepared for anything.

00:48:58.320 --> 00:49:06.040
I'd seen it all and nothing could upset me too much. Then this virus came along and threatened everyone in the world.

00:49:06.600 --> 00:49:11.080
Wow, that's a big deal, it's covering the entire planet.

00:49:13.560 --> 00:49:17.000
I don't know if it's happened to you, but it's happened to me.

00:49:17.280 --> 00:49:22.480
This is probably the ninth vice, which is envy; being

00:49:23.480 --> 00:49:25.680
happy when other people have problems.

00:49:25.680 --> 00:49:31.160
When I hear that famous, annoying people are sick.

00:49:32.120 --> 00:49:37.080
I don't want them to die or anything, but

00:49:37.960 --> 00:49:42.280
... I say it's bad to be bad.

00:49:43.000 --> 00:49:46.040
And then I catch myself thinking like that.

00:49:47.080 --> 00:49:49.120
It feels like a big deal.

00:49:49.480 --> 00:49:56.120
It feels like this problem has spread all over the planet.

00:49:57.080 --> 00:50:02.040
It feels like it's something that's hard for me to deal with.

00:50:02.520 --> 00:50:04.520
We've just entered,

00:50:04.600 --> 00:50:06.800
after 10 years of studying the lamrim,

00:50:08.040 --> 00:50:12.840
and we've actually been pointing the way for people with greater capacity.

00:50:13.840 --> 00:50:16.800
We're going to open that study

00:50:18.160 --> 00:50:21.200
with the idea of ​​bodhichitta. What is bodhichitta?

00:50:21.280 --> 00:50:27.000
It's not the enlightenment of the mind. Forget the bad translation, the translation is very good.  Bad.

00:50:27.960 --> 00:50:34.520
It's my hope that I can become a buddha to help countless sentient beings.

00:50:35.760 --> 00:50:37.960
There's that direct experience, just as

00:50:38.520 --> 00:50:41.600
there's the direct experience of emptiness.

00:50:41.600 --> 00:50:46.920
There's a parallel experience that

00:50:47.000 --> 00:50:53.080
we have to aim for in this life, and again, you have to be in meditation.

00:50:54.040 --> 00:51:00.960
We're describing an extraordinary... what you might call... breakthrough...

00:51:02.400 --> 00:51:06.040
threshold experience

00:51:07.080 --> 00:51:11.720
when you enter a deep state of meditation.

00:51:11.960 --> 00:51:15.480
Because space and time come from seeds,

00:51:15.760 --> 00:51:17.760
if you can play with these seeds,

00:51:18.040 --> 00:51:20.720
then you can package space and time.

00:51:21.480 --> 00:51:25.080
In a meditation that takes no more than half an hour,

00:51:26.520 --> 00:51:28.520
you can literally visit

00:51:28.720 --> 00:51:30.800
every person in the universe,

00:51:31.720 --> 00:51:34.440
including animals, insects, birds, and fish.

00:51:35.080 --> 00:51:39.400
You can communicate with each individual

00:51:40.040 --> 00:51:42.040
in that half hour.

00:51:42.120 --> 00:51:44.920
You can make a commitment to each one.

00:51:45.560 --> 00:51:50.160
You meet them, you see each person suffering,

00:51:50.400 --> 00:51:55.840
each one having a difficult life and worrying about the future.

00:51:56.400 --> 00:51:58.320
You can go to each one individually and say,

00:51:59.080 --> 00:52:01.880
"I'll take care of it, don't worry."

00:52:02.160 --> 00:52:04.560
I used to work when I was in university.

00:52:05.280 --> 00:52:08.440
I got a scholarship, but they said you had to work a certain number of hours a week.

00:52:09.000 --> 00:52:11.000
It turned out to be 30 hours a week.

00:52:12.160 --> 00:52:15.200
I had to drive a truck.

00:52:16.320 --> 00:52:21.200
Actually, at first they put me in  In the cafeteria, they said you'll be mopping the cafeteria floor.

00:52:21.280 --> 00:52:24.920
I quit after 10 hours. I quit the first day.

00:52:25.960 --> 00:52:29.760
Then they said, "You can drive a truck." I said, "That's fun. I'll drive a truck."

00:52:30.800 --> 00:52:33.520
I drove a truck for five years.

00:52:35.200 --> 00:52:37.560
There was a guy, a

00:52:37.960 --> 00:52:42.960
full-time employee of the university named Big John.

00:52:43.320 --> 00:52:49.240
His name was Big John. He was Polish, seven feet tall, a big guy.

00:52:50.800 --> 00:52:52.400
Everyone was scared when they saw him.

00:52:52.400 --> 00:52:56.120
They were afraid of him, but he was very sweet.

00:52:57.000 --> 00:53:02.840
He brought donuts to work, and he was from Trenton, New Jersey.

00:53:04.920 --> 00:53:10.320
He would do the best things for us and he would take care of us. One day we wrecked a truck.

00:53:11.000 --> 00:53:13.840
We hit a tree with the truck and we wrecked it.

00:53:14.440 --> 00:53:19.560
He took care of us, saying, "Oh, this screw wasn't tight enough.

00:53:19.560 --> 00:53:23.400
I don't know what happened. The truck is wrecked. Don't blame these guys.

00:53:24.160 --> 00:53:26.160
Don't blame this young man.

00:53:26.440 --> 00:53:28.440
They just drove it."

00:53:28.920 --> 00:53:33.080
Then he winked at us and said, "I've done you a favor."  I've helped you guys."

00:53:33.680 --> 00:53:37.040
I always think of him when I think of bodhichitta.

00:53:37.680 --> 00:53:42.000
You'll meet every living being in the universe face to face.

00:53:42.600 --> 00:53:46.600
And you'll say, "Big John has taken care of you.  I take care of you.  Don't worry.

00:53:47.200 --> 00:53:49.280
Don't think about it. I'm taking care of you.

00:53:50.320 --> 00:53:52.880
That's bodhichitta. You have to have that experience.

00:53:52.880 --> 00:53:55.680
You have to attain that experience. You have to meditate.

00:53:56.240 --> 00:53:58.080
You have to study bodhichitta.

00:53:58.080 --> 00:54:00.320
You have to study the lamrim of bodhichitta.

00:54:01.360 --> 00:54:03.400
You have to do all the steps;

00:54:04.480 --> 00:54:06.480
exchanging self and others...

00:54:07.000 --> 00:54:11.120
One day you will have that experience and you will meet every living being.

00:54:11.840 --> 00:54:15.280
You will say to them, 'I'm taking care of you.' Don't worry. I'm helping you.'

00:54:15.400 --> 00:54:20.040
Big Mike is taking care of you, or Big Tim, or Big Seiji.

00:54:20.600 --> 00:54:22.600
Don't worry.

00:54:23.080 --> 00:54:25.480
Don't stress. I'm on top of it! That's what it feels like

00:54:26.440 --> 00:54:30.040
. It's a personal commitment.

00:54:31.280 --> 00:54:33.280
Why are we talking about it?

00:54:33.840 --> 00:54:37.560
You'll do it in countless worlds. When you do it, the day you do it,

00:54:38.040 --> 00:54:40.520
you'll do it in countless worlds.

00:54:42.160 --> 00:54:48.320
An act done directly with every living being in countless worlds,

00:54:49.400 --> 00:54:54.160
no problem taking care of a single virus in a single world.

00:54:54.320 --> 00:54:55.440
It's nothing. A

00:54:55.760 --> 00:54:57.760
virus that harms

00:54:58.600 --> 00:55:03.680
7 or 8 billion people is nothing compared to bodhichitta.

00:55:04.960 --> 00:55:08.600
We say, if you spill ketchup on your shirt

00:55:08.600 --> 00:55:15.280
and take it to the middle of a 25 million-degree sun,

00:55:15.760 --> 00:55:18.720
maybe the ketchup stain will come off.

00:55:19.400 --> 00:55:24.240
You probably don't have to worry about the ketchup stain. Work on your bodhichitta.

00:55:25.400 --> 00:55:29.000
You'll destroy the virus, accidentally. It's

00:55:29.760 --> 00:55:31.760
no big deal.

00:55:32.120 --> 00:55:34.120
Next picture.

00:55:35.560 --> 00:55:38.120
Don't mess around with other paths.

00:55:38.920 --> 00:55:41.480
Learn bodhichitta. Learn to have this experience.

00:55:42.240 --> 00:55:44.240
Don't waste your time.

00:55:45.000 --> 00:55:47.680
Don't focus on anything else. Focus on bodhichitta.

00:55:48.800 --> 00:55:51.200
Then you won't have to do anything twice.

00:55:51.560 --> 00:55:55.200
We're talking about doing everything.  Twice. This woman was in a hurry.

00:55:55.680 --> 00:55:58.440
She said, I don't have time for this bodhichitta stuff.

00:55:59.000 --> 00:56:01.840
I'm going straight to tantra.

00:56:02.600 --> 00:56:06.120
You're still going to have to go back and get the thing you forgot,

00:56:06.120 --> 00:56:07.080
which is bodhichitta.

00:56:07.080 --> 00:56:09.360
Work on your bodhichitta first.

00:56:10.440 --> 00:56:16.160
You don't have to go back and get bodhichitta and go all the way.

00:56:20.320 --> 00:56:23.760
This is a radical example in the next picture.

00:56:29.000 --> 00:56:33.080
It's hard to remember. I'll give you some time to think about it.

00:56:43.840 --> 00:56:45.840
I don't know if you remember this.

00:56:48.040 --> 00:56:49.720
It's a bit complicated.

00:56:49.720 --> 00:56:59.160
A group of 60 men and women were about to attain nirvana just by seeing emptiness directly, and

00:56:59.320 --> 00:57:02.040
without bodhichitta, nirvana is lower.

00:57:03.680 --> 00:57:09.400
Manjushri appeared and taught them about bodhichitta.

00:57:09.520 --> 00:57:12.360
Maybe he was teaching them about the experience we just talked about.

00:57:14.720 --> 00:57:18.920
They were all upset with Manjushri. They were like, don't waste our time.

00:57:18.920 --> 00:57:22.160
We're close to nirvana. We can feel it. We can feel it.

00:57:22.920 --> 00:57:25.680
We've all seen emptiness, don't waste our time.

00:57:27.080 --> 00:57:31.160
Don't talk to us about this.

00:57:32.920 --> 00:57:37.520
Because they didn't respect the teachings about bodhichitta,

00:57:37.760 --> 00:57:42.160
they went to hell.

00:57:43.080 --> 00:57:46.040
They didn't go to heaven. They went to the realm of  hell.

00:57:47.080 --> 00:57:49.080
And they burned

00:57:50.040 --> 00:57:55.560
and they became humans again after millions of years.

00:57:57.840 --> 00:58:03.560
Deep inside were the bodhichitta teachings that Manjushri gave them and they remembered them.

00:58:04.240 --> 00:58:07.680
They become Bodhisattvas and they become Buddhas.

00:58:08.600 --> 00:58:10.600
It will take a shorter time, than

00:58:12.320 --> 00:58:16.320
going to lower nirvana without learning bodhichitta.

00:58:16.800 --> 00:58:20.800
It would be quicker to go to hell

00:58:20.800 --> 00:58:22.440
and come back

00:58:22.440 --> 00:58:25.080
and start again with bodhichitta,

00:58:25.960 --> 00:58:27.880
then if you don't use bodhichitta

00:58:27.880 --> 00:58:29.960
and you go to lower nirvana.

00:58:32.520 --> 00:58:37.120
This is a picture of someone misleading someone else on purpose.

00:58:38.720 --> 00:58:41.000
This woman asked;

00:58:41.000 --> 00:58:44.240
Which is the highway to the shop I want to visit?

00:58:45.000 --> 00:58:48.480
The man knew the highway was closed.

00:58:48.720 --> 00:58:52.240
He told him, 'Don't go through there because the highway is closed.  Go another way.

00:58:53.000 --> 00:58:55.000
And he insisted, 'No,

00:58:55.400 --> 00:58:57.400
tell me where the highway I want is.'

00:58:58.040 --> 00:58:59.840
Then he lied to her,

00:58:59.840 --> 00:59:06.120
saying, 'Take this path that's actually further, the one the man wants the woman to take.'

00:59:07.560 --> 00:59:10.600
This is a story about skillful means.

00:59:10.600 --> 00:59:12.160
Next picture.

00:59:17.280 --> 00:59:21.400
This is a warm-up before you enter a race.

00:59:23.560 --> 00:59:27.560
Usually, what do we use this picture for? Do you remember?

00:59:29.000 --> 00:59:31.040
It's breath meditation.

00:59:31.400 --> 00:59:36.800
Usually, we say breath meditation is a warm-up. Don't think of it as a race.

00:59:37.960 --> 00:59:44.160
In the Olympics, there's no contest for stretching before a race. There's

00:59:44.160 --> 00:59:48.440
no such thing; you don't get a gold medal for stretching.

00:59:49.400 --> 00:59:54.480
In this case, we're not talking about breath meditation. We're talking about, it's

00:59:54.640 --> 00:59:59.840
better to do the three main paths in sequence.

01:00:01.080 --> 01:00:03.080
Feeling sad about this world.

01:00:05.960 --> 01:00:09.120
Striving to have a direct experience of bodhichitta.

01:00:09.800 --> 01:00:12.680
Seeing emptiness so you can help everyone.

01:00:13.160 --> 01:00:18.880
Warming up by feeling sad about this life first.

01:00:19.000 --> 01:00:21.440
Next picture.

01:00:24.040 --> 01:00:29.960
We're almost done. I think we're very close. Are we close? Not that close. Okay.

01:00:32.040 --> 01:00:35.760
Do you remember who these guys are? They're a really bad band.

01:00:36.520 --> 01:00:41.200
I guess you met them at a shopping mall or something, singing bad songs.

01:00:45.080 --> 01:00:47.000
They're called, 'the opening act.'

01:00:47.760 --> 01:00:49.760
Step on the path to a lower capacity;

01:00:51.200 --> 01:00:53.120
try to  Getting a higher rebirth.

01:00:53.120 --> 01:00:55.560
Stepping on the path to medium capacity,

01:00:56.160 --> 01:00:58.160
trying not to return to this world at all.

01:00:59.080 --> 01:01:02.120
Stepping on the path to greater capacity.

01:01:02.120 --> 01:01:03.080
These two levels are just the opening acts.

01:01:03.840 --> 01:01:10.440
This is the main thing, leading to bodhichitta. What's above bodhichitta?

01:01:13.280 --> 01:01:16.720
There are six perfections. Check them out:

01:01:19.000 --> 01:01:21.000
steps on the path to keeping your ass

01:01:21.200 --> 01:01:25.800
out of the lower hells, steps on the path to getting to nirvana,

01:01:26.920 --> 01:01:29.080
and then we have bodhichitta.

01:01:29.240 --> 01:01:30.320
This is the experience of meeting every sentient being

01:01:30.320 --> 01:01:35.400
and making a commitment that I will take care of you.

01:01:36.120 --> 01:01:38.120
Up here is the sixth.

01:01:38.120 --> 01:01:41.080
That's six in Chinese.

01:01:42.160 --> 01:01:45.400
Up here are the six perfections.

01:01:46.240 --> 01:01:47.400
Now, which one is the big deal? Which one is the

01:01:47.400 --> 01:01:52.240
real band? Which one is the opening act?

01:01:54.920 --> 01:01:56.920
These people are clear, lower nirvana is no big deal.

01:01:57.680 --> 01:01:59.680
What's interesting is, Pabongka Rinpoche said,

01:02:00.680 --> 01:02:03.480
that experience

01:02:04.120 --> 01:02:06.120
with every sentient being

01:02:06.240 --> 01:02:07.400
is the main act.

01:02:07.400 --> 01:02:09.120
That's the focus I want you to have.

01:02:09.120 --> 01:02:11.200
I want you to try to have that experience.

01:02:12.160 --> 01:02:16.040
If you have that experience, we can talk about the six perfections,

01:02:16.040 --> 01:02:19.960
including number six, which is seeing emptiness.

01:02:20.600 --> 01:02:22.600
We'll talk about that later.

01:02:23.080 --> 01:02:26.040
Come on, I want you to focus on this experience.

01:02:27.000 --> 01:02:33.080
By the way, a good way  To have that experience is to imagine the experience and try to listen to the description.

01:02:34.040 --> 01:02:36.920
Pretend you can do it and keep pretending.

01:02:37.680 --> 01:02:39.200
Keep doing it.

01:02:39.200 --> 01:02:44.160
It feels like a slot machine.

01:02:44.440 --> 01:02:46.560
I want to say, it feels like a slot machine.

01:02:47.640 --> 01:02:49.560
When you push the button on a slot machine,

01:02:50.040 --> 01:02:52.040
these pictures spin;

01:02:52.720 --> 01:02:54.280
cherries, and other pictures.

01:02:54.280 --> 01:02:58.800
Not that I've ever played a slot machine. Well, once, with my dad.

01:02:59.840 --> 01:03:02.840
You push the stick and then the numbers move like this.

01:03:02.840 --> 01:03:04.800
Just imagine

01:03:04.920 --> 01:03:06.920
your mom's face coming up.

01:03:07.760 --> 01:03:12.520
You say, 'Your mom looks worried.' She's like, 'Yeah, I'm worried about life.'

01:03:12.520 --> 01:03:16.480
You say, 'Don't worry, Big John's got you covered.'

01:03:16.840 --> 01:03:19.200
Relax. I understand. I'm on top of it.

01:03:20.040 --> 01:03:22.040
Then a picture of your father appears.

01:03:23.000 --> 01:03:27.360
Not just the picture, but the person appears.

01:03:27.760 --> 01:03:31.360
It feels like that in meditation. Try to imagine it. Try to practice.

01:03:31.560 --> 01:03:33.560
It will trigger the real thing.

01:03:34.320 --> 01:03:37.280
It will trigger the real thing. Bring people in, one by one.

01:03:38.040 --> 01:03:40.040
See how they feel.

01:03:40.040 --> 01:03:43.160
Make a commitment. Don't worry. I'm taking care of you. I'm on top of it.

01:03:43.160 --> 01:03:45.200
Then they pass. Bring someone else in.

01:03:46.240 --> 01:03:49.480
Practice like that. You can do five or six people.

01:03:50.520 --> 01:03:54.080
It will get faster, because times will change.

01:03:54.600 --> 01:04:00.040
Pabongka Rinpoche said that was the main act.

01:04:01.000 --> 01:04:02.800
It was the Rolling Stones.

01:04:03.080 --> 01:04:09.240
The others were just new bands that weren't very good.

01:04:10.520 --> 01:04:13.960
Who was the last one? Did they have a final act? Usually not.

01:04:14.800 --> 01:04:18.920
Anyway, the rest just left the stadium or something. Never mind.

01:04:20.600 --> 01:04:22.600
Now we're moving on to the

01:04:23.200 --> 01:04:26.480
10 cool things about gaining bodhichitta.

01:04:26.640 --> 01:04:30.040
We'll only have time to do the first one in this lamrim. The

01:04:30.440 --> 01:04:33.280
first cool thing about gaining bodhichitta is...

01:04:34.040 --> 01:04:36.320
if you were a nerd

01:04:37.280 --> 01:04:39.280
who played tennis in school.

01:04:39.960 --> 01:04:42.840
Your dream was to be on the team.

01:04:43.120 --> 01:04:44.440
Next picture.

01:04:47.640 --> 01:04:50.000
Yes, there's Geshe Michael in the middle.

01:04:50.000 --> 01:04:52.880
At the top, isn't it?  The strange people below.

01:04:54.320 --> 01:05:00.800
You can join the team. It's great to be on the Bodhisattva team.

01:05:02.600 --> 01:05:04.600
Work to be on that team. It's

01:05:04.720 --> 01:05:09.000
really cool to be on that team,

01:05:09.400 --> 01:05:11.840
because it spans the universe.

01:05:12.440 --> 01:05:16.960
It's all these cool people all over the universe. It's really cool to be part of that team.

01:05:17.080 --> 01:05:18.760
It's sweet.

01:05:19.560 --> 01:05:24.120
That's the first benefit of bodhichitta.

01:05:24.680 --> 01:05:25.920
Next picture:

01:05:28.160 --> 01:05:30.320
This is a man visiting an art museum.

01:05:32.920 --> 01:05:38.640
He talks about two levels of tantra: the first level is meeting angels, and the

01:05:39.960 --> 01:05:43.320
second level is studying how to become angels and become angels.

01:05:43.320 --> 01:05:44.800
In the first level,

01:05:45.680 --> 01:05:47.680
we're supposed to actually meet

01:05:48.120 --> 01:05:50.120
real angels in person.

01:05:50.720 --> 01:05:58.720
It's not like standing in an art museum and looking at a statue or a thangka of someone.

01:05:59.040 --> 01:06:05.720
This is meeting them in person, and that's a completely different thing.

01:06:07.280 --> 01:06:09.720
If you try to practice tantra

01:06:10.080 --> 01:06:15.480
without the experience of bodhichitta, it's like looking at a picture of Buddha

01:06:15.480 --> 01:06:17.400
instead of meeting Buddha.

01:06:17.720 --> 01:06:22.960
They don't like talking to people who don't have bodhichitta.

01:06:22.960 --> 01:06:24.320
They feel more comfortable

01:06:24.520 --> 01:06:28.040
around people who have this experience. Try to have this experience.

01:06:28.600 --> 01:06:30.280
Then tantra will work for you.

01:06:30.280 --> 01:06:32.160
If you don't have this experience,

01:06:32.200 --> 01:06:34.360
tantra will be difficult.

01:06:34.360 --> 01:06:39.200
It's like looking at pictures of Buddhas instead of meeting them.  They.

01:06:40.040 --> 01:06:42.040
Next.

01:06:45.280 --> 01:06:51.120
If you try to practice tantra without bodhichitta, you might get bad results.

01:06:51.320 --> 01:06:54.200
We're talking about the first nuclear tests

01:06:54.440 --> 01:06:56.480
in modern times.

01:06:59.080 --> 01:07:04.800
Scientists acknowledged that this explosion

01:07:04.920 --> 01:07:07.480
might ignite the entire world.

01:07:07.480 --> 01:07:09.840
They were just trying to do something cool.

01:07:10.920 --> 01:07:13.600
But they were gambling with a major disaster.

01:07:14.240 --> 01:07:17.680
That's tantra without bodhichitta.

01:07:18.040 --> 01:07:23.720
It's like accidentally setting the sky on fire. You're going to mess it up.

01:07:23.960 --> 01:07:25.680
Next.

01:07:28.120 --> 01:07:32.880
Even small, neutral karma

01:07:33.040 --> 01:07:36.960
becomes powerful for someone with bodhichitta.

01:07:37.080 --> 01:07:39.080
Someone with bodhichitta can feed the birds,

01:07:39.400 --> 01:07:41.440
make a prayer about it,

01:07:41.600 --> 01:07:46.840
and influence millions of people. They have this power.

01:07:46.840 --> 01:07:48.600
Next picture.

01:07:51.680 --> 01:07:59.120
Even a small bad deed like stealing French fries to feed the birds can become powerful if done by a bodhisattva.

01:08:00.600 --> 01:08:08.040
But this is a dangerous practice. We're not at that level. We're not at that level. We're not at that level.

01:08:08.720 --> 01:08:10.720
You hear that? No?

01:08:10.800 --> 01:08:12.800
We have a picture of

01:08:13.400 --> 01:08:15.400
fugu fish.

01:08:16.040 --> 01:08:21.200
People in Japan, like macho men, eat this fish.

01:08:22.040 --> 01:08:28.040
There are very, very poisonous parts that can kill you instantly. 50 people a year die in Japan.

01:08:29.080 --> 01:08:34.080
But people still go to restaurants. They serve this fish.  In a restaurant,

01:08:34.720 --> 01:08:38.240
you need three years of special training or you'll kill someone.

01:08:39.080 --> 01:08:42.120
It's like stealing French fries to give them to a bird

01:08:43.400 --> 01:08:45.200
because you want to help the bird.

01:08:45.200 --> 01:08:51.240
We're not at that level. Don't eat fugu if you're not trained.

01:08:52.440 --> 01:08:54.440
Then we have this great picture of Nick and Erin

01:08:54.920 --> 01:08:58.120
with their big boss,

01:08:59.080 --> 01:09:01.360
Amalie.

01:09:02.120 --> 01:09:04.320
Amalie represents the Buddha,

01:09:05.480 --> 01:09:06.800
and Nick

01:09:06.800 --> 01:09:08.800
represents the father,

01:09:09.400 --> 01:09:14.240
which is bodhichitta, and Erin represents wisdom,

01:09:14.440 --> 01:09:16.920
which is the direct perception of emptiness.

01:09:16.920 --> 01:09:18.920
In some way,

01:09:20.800 --> 01:09:25.800
somehow, I don't know what this belief is in Asia, but in some way the father is irreplaceable. There's

01:09:28.040 --> 01:09:30.040
something special about the father.

01:09:33.400 --> 01:09:35.400
I don't know what it is. But anyway...

01:09:36.960 --> 01:09:39.840
You can see emptiness at different levels,

01:09:40.600 --> 01:09:42.800
on all three tracks.

01:09:43.480 --> 01:09:46.240
But bodhichitta, you have to be special.

01:09:47.080 --> 01:09:49.080
You can only see it on the highest track.

01:09:49.760 --> 01:09:51.680
Define yourself

01:09:51.680 --> 01:09:53.680
as someone on the higher track.

01:09:54.120 --> 01:09:57.600
You need both to have a baby who is Buddhahood.

01:09:59.080 --> 01:10:01.080
Next picture.

01:10:04.440 --> 01:10:10.040
We said thuk dam gyi thil. The

01:10:10.600 --> 01:10:13.680
Yang Team correctly identified today.

01:10:14.720 --> 01:10:21.600
What is your main practice? What is the number one thing in your life right now?

01:10:21.600 --> 01:10:27.360
Until the next lamrim, Medicine Buddha lamrim.  ..

01:10:28.040 --> 01:10:31.600
...I want you to treat this as your main practice.

01:10:31.600 --> 01:10:34.320
Try to have the experience of meeting countless beings.

01:10:34.320 --> 01:10:36.800
Try to have that experience.

01:10:36.800 --> 01:10:40.040
I don't care if you sit there for hours and nothing happens,

01:10:40.920 --> 01:10:42.920
just try, just pretend.

01:10:43.080 --> 01:10:47.080
Get into your mind until the next lamrim.

01:10:47.080 --> 01:10:51.200
Let's make a deal like that. Make it your main practice.

01:10:52.120 --> 01:10:54.120
Next picture.

01:10:56.240 --> 01:11:02.600
If the practice wasn't so important then one of the greatest Buddhists of all time, Lord Atisha, wouldn't have sailed for

01:11:02.800 --> 01:11:06.240
13 months risking his life to get the teachings on

01:11:06.880 --> 01:11:08.880
bodhichitta that you just got

01:11:09.080 --> 01:11:12.920
in this video. And you don't have to go anywhere.

01:11:13.840 --> 01:11:18.920
If Atisha thought it was worth risking his life for 13 months

01:11:19.840 --> 01:11:21.680
on a small boat

01:11:21.680 --> 01:11:25.760
in the Pacific Ocean and the Indian Ocean, then maybe

01:11:26.440 --> 01:11:30.040
it's important, maybe it's worth it.

01:11:30.040 --> 01:11:31.560
Next picture.

01:11:34.800 --> 01:11:40.240
I think the stupidest thing you can do in your entire life is to go to Paris and not buy a croissant.

01:11:41.680 --> 01:11:46.440
Okay. I'm just saying, there are probably other stupid things you can do in life.

01:11:46.760 --> 01:11:48.920
But to me the stupidest thing

01:11:48.920 --> 01:11:52.800
is to go to Paris and not go to a bakery? At least

01:11:54.040 --> 01:11:55.840
buy one.  A crepe

01:11:55.840 --> 01:11:57.840
on the street

01:11:57.960 --> 01:12:00.200
with... what chocolate is that?

01:12:02.800 --> 01:12:04.320
Nutella, yes.

01:12:04.320 --> 01:12:06.320
There is no Nutella crepe.

01:12:07.000 --> 01:12:12.760
To go to Paris and not eat a Nutella crepe is to prove you're crazy.

01:12:15.040 --> 01:12:17.200
If you study the lamrim,

01:12:17.400 --> 01:12:21.960
if you've gotten this far in the lamrim, and Geshela has been teaching for 10 years,

01:12:22.800 --> 01:12:25.400
you eventually get to the croissant,

01:12:26.040 --> 01:12:28.040
which is the bodhisattva experience.

01:12:28.720 --> 01:12:35.960
Don't be crazy and leave Paris without eating one. Don't leave the lamrim without having this experience.

01:12:36.160 --> 01:12:38.040
You're an idiot.

01:12:41.680 --> 01:12:46.080
We're done with the croissant. I thought you wanted to make a presentation?

01:12:48.320 --> 01:12:52.040
No, I guess there might be a croissant in that bag?

01:12:54.320 --> 01:12:56.320
Tim Lowenhaupt

01:12:57.080 --> 01:12:59.560
is going to make a formal presentation

01:13:00.800 --> 01:13:02.720
for Geshela, my pay.

01:13:03.840 --> 01:13:07.400
Oh, that's a pande? What do you call it?

01:13:10.520 --> 01:13:12.520
What's it called? This

01:13:14.320 --> 01:13:18.560
chocolate pande here. You have to divide it into three pieces.

01:13:20.120 --> 01:13:22.320
And give me all three, I mean no, just one.

01:13:23.760 --> 01:13:26.080
I have a chocolate pande.

01:13:27.000 --> 01:13:30.240
This is what you give your teachers when they teach you about bodhichitta.

01:13:31.080 --> 01:13:33.200
Let's make a deal.

01:13:34.160 --> 01:13:36.040
For the next few months

01:13:37.000 --> 01:13:41.760
work on that experience. Do the chapters.  Dedicate yourself to your Shantideva meditation.

01:13:43.680 --> 01:13:48.600
Try to work towards having that experience. The worst that can happen, at least

01:13:49.400 --> 01:13:52.440
you'll have planted the seed in your mind for having this experience.

01:13:53.280 --> 01:13:55.080
Just pretend.

01:13:55.080 --> 01:13:59.680
Just sit and fantasize about it. Fantasizing is a great meditation.

01:14:00.880 --> 01:14:03.000
Fantasize that you're having this experience of meeting,

01:14:03.840 --> 01:14:05.080
one by one,

01:14:05.080 --> 01:14:06.640
every sentient being.

01:14:06.640 --> 01:14:10.160
You're making a personal commitment with each one

01:14:10.800 --> 01:14:13.400
to take care of them in the best way possible.

01:14:14.160 --> 01:14:18.080
Okay. See you at the next lamrim for Medicine Buddha. Yay!

